{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Functional"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/factorykit\/functional"]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Functional Injection","modules":[{"name":"FactoryKit"}]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Factory can inject more than service classes and structs."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Advanced-Topics","title":"Advanced Topics","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Modifiers","doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Actors","doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Modules","doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Scenes","doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Cycle","doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Optionals","doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Tags"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Functional Injection is a powerful tool that can, in many cases, eliminate the need for defining protocols, implementations, and the various stubs and mocks one needs when doing traditional Protocol-Oriented-Programing.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Example","anchor":"Example"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Consider the following typealias and Factory.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["typealias AccountProviding = () async throws -> [Account]","","extension Container {","    var accountProvider: Factory<AccountProviding> {","        self {{ try await Network.get(path: \"\/accounts\") }}","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Note the double braces. In this example our factory closure is returning a closure, not a class or struct.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Now, here’s the view model that uses it.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["class AccountViewModel: ObservableObject {","    @Injected(\\.accountProvider) var accountProvider","    @Published var accounts: [Account] = []","    @MainActor func load() async {","        do {","            accounts = try await accountProvider()","        } catch {","            print(error)","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Testing","anchor":"Testing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Now consider how easy it is to write a test with mock accounts…","type":"text"}]},{"code":["func testAllAccounts() async {","    Container.shared.accountProvider.register {{ Account.mockAccounts }}","    do {","        let viewModel = AccountViewModel()","        try await viewModel.load()","        XCTAssert(viewModel.accounts.count == 5)","    } catch {","        XCTFail(\"Account load failed\")","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Or test edge cases like no accounts found.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["func testEmptyAccounts() async {","    Container.shared.accountProvider.register {{ [] }}","    ...","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Or test specific error cases."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["func testErrorLoadingAccounts() async {","    Container.shared.accountProvider.register {{ throw APIError.network }}","    ...","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Here’s an article that goes into the technique in more detail: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/betterprogramming.pub\/factory-and-functional-dependency-injection-2d0a38042d05","type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://FactoryKit/documentation/FactoryKit/Cycle":{"url":"\/documentation\/factorykit\/cycle","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What’s a resolution cycle, and why should we care?"}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Cycle","type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Resolution Cycles"},"doc://FactoryKit/documentation/FactoryKit/Modules":{"url":"\/documentation\/factorykit\/modules","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Using Factory in a project with multiple modules."}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Modules","type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Modular Development"},"doc://FactoryKit/documentation/FactoryKit":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit","type":"topic","title":"FactoryKit","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A modern approach to Container-Based Dependency Injection for Swift and SwiftUI."}],"url":"\/documentation\/factorykit","kind":"symbol"},"doc://FactoryKit/documentation/FactoryKit/Scenes":{"url":"\/documentation\/factorykit\/scenes","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Giving every window its own container instead of sharing one global."}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Scenes","type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Per-Scene Containers"},"doc://FactoryKit/documentation/FactoryKit/Tags":{"url":"\/documentation\/factorykit\/tags","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Obtaining a list of dependencies of a given type."}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Tags","type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Tags"},"doc://FactoryKit/documentation/FactoryKit/Optionals":{"url":"\/documentation\/factorykit\/optionals","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"With Factory registrations can be performed at any time."}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Optionals","type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Optionals and Dynamic Registration"},"https://betterprogramming.pub/factory-and-functional-dependency-injection-2d0a38042d05":{"titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Factory and Functional Dependency Injection","type":"text"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/betterprogramming.pub\/factory-and-functional-dependency-injection-2d0a38042d05","type":"link","title":"Factory and Functional Dependency Injection","url":"https:\/\/betterprogramming.pub\/factory-and-functional-dependency-injection-2d0a38042d05"},"doc://FactoryKit/documentation/FactoryKit/Modifiers":{"url":"\/documentation\/factorykit\/modifiers","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Considerations when defining and redefining a Factory’s behavior."}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Modifiers","type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Factory Modifiers"},"doc://FactoryKit/documentation/FactoryKit/Actors":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Actors","url":"\/documentation\/factorykit\/actors","title":"Actors and Actor Isolation","type":"topic","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Registering and resolving actors and actor-isolated dependencies."}],"kind":"article"}}}